10 Terraform Scenarios Every DevOps Engineer Must Know !!!

	1.	State file deleted → Terraform forgets infra, tries to recreate.
👉 Use remote backend with versioning.

	2.	Multiple applies at once → State corruption & drift.
👉 Use state locking.

	3.	Resource fails mid-apply → Partial infra + tainted resources.
👉 Re-run apply or taint/replace.

	4.	AWS rate limits → Throttling errors, partial deployment.
👉 Lower parallelism or raise limits.

	5.	Infra changed outside Terraform → Drift hidden until refresh.
👉 Treat Terraform as single source of truth.

	6.	Resource removed from config → Terraform destroys it.
👉 Use prevent_destroy or state rm.

	7.	Provider/API change → Plans break, forced recreation.
👉 Pin provider versions, test upgrades.

	8.	Circular dependencies → Plan fails with cycle error.
👉 Refactor modules, break loops.

	9.	AWS quotas exceeded → Resource creation fails.
👉 Monitor & request quota increases early.

	10.	Lost remote state access → No safe changes possible.
👉 Secure & back up state backend.
